  "content": {
    "id": "p18-p5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\left(\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{e^x+e^{-x}}\\right)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1$\n\nDivide the numerator and denominator by $e^x$, then use $e^{-2x}\\to0$.",
      "worked": "Divide the numerator and denominator by $e^x$. As $x\\to\\infty$, $e^{-2x}\\to 0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{e^x+e^{-x}}&=\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{1-e^{-2x}}{1+e^{-2x}}\\\\\n\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{e^x+e^{-x}}&=\\frac{1-0}{1+0}\\\\\n\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{e^x+e^{-x}}&=1\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 20
  },
